      "writtenOn": "2024-08-13T04:03:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "@smoreland@google.com, to clarify the purpose of the change a little bit - I don\u0027t think it\u0027s for exemption of a specific project but exemption of partner APEXs in that\n- for the Google-owned APEXs in our project, we would still follow the normal process of APEX availability\n- for the partner-owned APEXs, we apply for exemption because we don\u0027t know their names and it requires all the dependencies to be \u0027apex_available: //anyapex\u0027 which is not pleasant for the majority libraries that allow making copies. I would assume the same situation also applies to other partner APEXs.\n\nAt the same time, @jooyung@google.com @jiyong@google.com, do you see any concern if we replace the ENFORCE_APEX_AVAILABILITY_NAMESPACE_LIST with **DISABLE**_ENFORCE_APEX_AVAILABILITY_NAMESPACE_LIST?",
      "parentUuid": "d7a6e842_592cf048",
      "revId": "484873a872ac30e5cb735f06536d34a5d59fcb57",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1bb37ebc_128c4d8b",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1415877
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-13T05:07:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I understand Steven\u0027s concern and agree with it. However, I don\u0027t think `DISABLE_ENFORCE_APEX_AVAILABILITY_NAMESPACE_LIST` would work because those apexes will fail the checks when building other targets that doesn\u0027t set the variable.\n\nSteven suggested an interesting idea: `//apex_available:partnerapex`. And I think this would be better because it gives library owners a change to think about apex-availability. We can think of `partnerapex` as a pseudoname for non-AOSP APEXes (not starting with `com.android.`).\n\nChan and Jiyong, what do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "a773bbb3_f139c60a",
      "revId": "484873a872ac30e5cb735f06536d34a5d59fcb57",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
